# mm.audio.es8311

The EverAs ast ES8311 audio codec, its DAC as a playback output. It is
programmed over portable mm.mcu I2C and plays over portable mm.mcu I2S. It
contains no vendor header and no board pin number: a provider supplies the
wiring and this module drives the protocol.

Modelled on the mainline Linux ASoC driver for this codec. The codec answers on
an eight-bit register and eight-bit value I2C bus, and is identified by the
address its provider assigns rather than by a chip identifier register, which is
how that driver probes it. initialize performs the driver's reset and power-up
sequence and programs the output channel for I2S playback; play ships the
caller's samples down the I2S link as sixteen-bit little-endian bytes.

Two things in that driver are deliberately not reproduced. Its clock dividers,
which turn the board's master clock into the bit and word clocks, are absent,
because they depend on the master clock a board provides; the I2S link's baud is
what this module controls. Its ADC and microphone path is absent, because this
module is the output end and the input is mm.audio's microphone.
